35182	news	https://nairametrics.com/2026/08/08/tyms-brings-accounting-and-bookkeeping-to-claude-and-chatgpt/	Tyms Brings Accounting and Bookkeeping to Claude and ChatGPT <p>Business owners can now ask an AI assistant what their books look like and get an answer from their actual numbers. Most business owners do not have a finance team. They have a rough sense of what came in this month, a folder of receipts, and a nagging feeling that the real picture is somewhere [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://nairametrics.com/2026/08/08/tyms-brings-accounting-and-bookkeeping-to-claude-and-chatgpt/">Tyms Brings Accounting and Bookkeeping to Claude and ChatGPT</a> appeared first on <a href="https://nairametrics.com">Nairametrics</a>.</p>	https://nairametrics.com/2026/08/08/tyms-brings-accounting-and-bookkeeping-to-claude-and-chatgpt/	en	2026-08-08 11:00:13+00	2026-08-09 22:39:20.84675+00	nairametrics:Nigeria diaspora community UK
35183	news	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/present-but-displaced-what-western-objections-to-reparations-fail-to-see/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=present-but-displaced-what-western-objections-	Present but Displaced: What Western Objections to Reparations Fail to See <p>On 25 March 2026, the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) adopted a Ghana-led resolution declaring the trafficking and racialised chattel enslavement of Africans the gravest crime against humanity. It passed by 123 votes to three, with 52 abstentions. Argentina, Israel and the United States voted against it, while the United Kingdom and European Union member states abstained. The resolution forms part of an African–Caribbean effort to move reparatory justice from advocacy into international diplomacy. Importantly, it did not create a tribunal, name liable states or order transfers. Instead, the resolution called for dialogue on apologies, restitution, compensation, rehabilitation, cultural property [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/present-but-displaced-what-western-objections-to-reparations-fail-to-see/">Present but Displaced: What Western Objections to Reparations Fail to See</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/present-but-displaced-what-western-objections-to-reparations-fail-to-see/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=present-but-displaced-what-western-objections-to-reparations-fail-to-see	en	2026-08-09 14:28:31+00	2026-08-09 22:39:21.02153+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK
35184	news	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/what-young-kenyan-men-say-when-no-one-is-watching/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=what-young-kenyan-men-say-when-no-one-is-watching	What young Kenyan men say when no one is watching <p>A young Kenyan man recently sent this anonymous message to a chatbot late at night: “Mbogi wanasema mimi si mwanaume nisipolala na huyo mama… tangu lini mtu ashajiita mwanaume kwa sababu ya kulala na wanawake?” (“My crew tells me I’m not a man if I don’t sleep with her. Since when did sleeping with women make someone a man?”) That single sentence may explain more about the state of masculinity in Kenya today than many formal reports ever could. The message came through Sema na Me, an AI-enabled WhatsApp companion developed by Shujaaz Inc. that allows young people to anonymously [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/what-young-kenyan-men-say-when-no-one-is-watching/">What young Kenyan men say when no one is watching</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/what-young-kenyan-men-say-when-no-one-is-watching/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=what-young-kenyan-men-say-when-no-one-is-watching	en	2026-08-09 14:15:59+00	2026-08-09 22:39:21.046277+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK
